{
  "_": "Screen list for the JS-to-Unity parity harness. tools/js-reference-capture.mjs captures every id from the HTML/JS game; the Unity captures (Unity/Assets/AshenSpire/Tests/PlayMode/ScreenCaptureTests.cs in the editor, tools/unity-parity-capture.mjs against a WebGL player) replay each id's `unity.steps` and write the same file names; tools/parity-report.mjs pairs them. `unity: null` means Unity has no equivalent screen yet (`pending` says which port phase adds it). `dom` lists JS selectors whose rects and computed styles are dumped; `pairs` maps a JS selector to a Unity control name for layout-rect deltas. Step vocabulary is documented in DEVELOPER.md (Parity harness).",
